{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D31-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"02c0ecbbf5998fedc5b948c60be3ac04c10501a88d2052008a1cfcd3bd8fc64d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 recruits corroboration about Alex's bin duty; A3 and A5 manufacture support for that allocation.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's conflicting recollection prompts A3's new rota; B4's ignorance prompts A5 to establish the conversation now.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 remembers A being responsible and B4 questions the supposed agreement, complicating recruitment.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves from citing a past agreement in A3 to creating one that B must remember confidently.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives a house meeting, named housemate and bin duty; A3 supplies the rota dispute.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'We're having it now' economically converts B4's question into the attempted corroboration.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"At the house meeting, back me up about the bins being Alex's turn.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I thought it was yours.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Only on the old rota. Remember the new conversation?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There was a new conversation?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We're having it now. Try to remember it confidently.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recruits a housemate to corroborate A's preferred allocation of an ordinary shared responsibility.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"This could resemble generic lying or avoiding chores unless recruiting B's support remains central.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 explicitly asks B to back the bin-duty account, and A5 recruits B's confident recollection rather than merely denying responsibility.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a tries to manufacture a shared agreement; alternative b bargains down to silent support after an explicit ethical refusal.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged. Internal reread confirms the original ratings and 90 total: B2 and B4 each force a new recruitment tactic, and the five spoken turns satisfy the gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's 'new conversation' is deliberately slippery, and the scene emphasizes dishonest corroboration more than negotiating a fair rota.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D31-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"849a2e03576398e11fab6af001bd2db961f0204285696e427f8313e57a81160c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 seeks support for a morning-shift agreement; A5 still seeks visible corroboration of that account.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's absence becomes A3's lack of conflicting memory; B4's refusal to lie makes A5 request silence with a supportive expression.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 establishes an ethical boundary that changes what A can ask this coworker to do.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 makes a more precisely calibrated recruitment attempt after B4 rules out spoken lying.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a manager, shift coverage and a disputed agreement without extra explanation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'no conflicting memory' and A5's 'thoughtfully unsurprised' follow the same opportunistic logic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tell the manager we agreed I'd cover the morning, not the evening.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I wasn't in that meeting.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then you have no conflicting memory.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm not lying for you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you look thoughtfully unsurprised while I explain?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recruits a coworker's support for A's version of an ordinary shift-covering agreement.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Evading an unwanted shift is adjacent, but the requested behavior specifically requires recruiting another person's corroboration.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks B to tell the manager, and A5 preserves B's supporting role even after B4 refuses to lie.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b adapts to a coworker's moral boundary through nonverbal support; alternative a tries to create a housemate's supporting memory.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged. Internal reread confirms the original six ratings and 90 total; A5's narrower request directly needs B4's refusal, and all dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final request is spoken character dialogue, not an action paragraph, but its success in performance depends on keeping A earnest.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D32-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"594e8992bbf1a47f4c1bc2d5e8aef0c10e2ef9375a2a1ef56a60e3046479538c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 asks B to try an uncertain tap repair; A5 keeps A away from the actual test.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's spray concern informs A3's tiles suggestion, and B4's reversal prompts A5's observation excuse.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 fears getting sprayed and B4 asks A to bear the test, giving B a credible objection.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats A1's vague 'important thing' without increasing the practical stakes or refining the test much.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes the repaired tap and A3 wet tiles, though 'point it' leaves the fixture's movement unclear.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's distant observation excuse is concise and belongs to A's wish to delegate the test.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 83\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Turn the kitchen tap on before I start washing up. I've tightened the loose joint.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It sprayed me last time.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Wear my apron. I need to know whether the joint holds.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You wear it and turn the tap.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll need it dry for washing up. You can have my raincoat for the test.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A gets B to test an uncertain repair before A relies on it for washing up.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simply delegating an unpleasant chore would not require a trial whose result determines A's later use.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 requests a repair test; revised A1 explicitly makes testing precede washing up, and A3 identifies the joint being tested.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses protective equipment to bargain around a previous soaking; alternative b uses a shared coffee budget to recruit a taste tester.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the kitchen setting to clarify the test and later reliance. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 test before washing), logic 5 (B2 prompts protection; B4 prompts reserving the apron), relationship 4 (B resists another soaking), heightening 4 (A5 offers stronger protection while keeping B the tester), specificity 5 (loose joint and washing up), brevityWit 4 (dry-apron rationale). Total 92; five spoken turns, 66 words, gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's dry-apron argument is transparently self-serving; A must believe the equipment bargain is reasonable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D32-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"63ed41ca63e07680ab38b61c7d5030d33b5b3de362b5233f1f8acff2e17a04f2\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 explicitly asks B to taste a substitute before A fills a cup; A5 preserves B as the first tester.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 evasively answers B2's ingredients question; A5 uses B4's discovery that A has not tasted it.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 inquire but supply little personal reason to cooperate or refuse.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 relabels the same tasting request as an 'independent assessment' without adding a consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's cheap coffee substitute and unfilled cup establish an immediately playable test.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's uninformative 'blend' and A5's formal flattery are compact expressions of evasion.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 80\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Taste this cheap coffee substitute before I fill my cup.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We still have proper coffee.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"If you like this, we can save the proper stuff for guests.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm not sacrificing breakfast to save you money.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One sip. If it's awful, I'll buy you a croissant and keep my cup empty.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recruits B to sample a cheaper substitute before deciding whether to drink it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Selling someone a cheaper product is adjacent, but A must use B's prior test to protect A's own choice.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 specifies tasting before A fills a cup; revised A5 makes a failed test leave A's cup empty.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b offers compensation for a small sensory trial; alternative a offers protection against the physical consequences of a repair test.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the same coffee situation to give B a breakfast preference and A a bargain. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 and A5 preserve prior testing), logic 5 (B2 supplies the reserve coffee; B4 causes the croissant offer), relationship 4 (B values breakfast), heightening 4 (A5 accepts a cost while preserving the test), specificity 4 (guest coffee and croissant), brevityWit 4 (empty cup exposes A's terms). Total 90; five spoken turns, 64 words, gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The compensation is modest rather than a large comic escalation; its strength is a clearer negotiation and conditional reliance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D33-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"63f954019e3423866e964e773e266e662957d6dc33c6312657294f93781b6ec8\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands recognition of the bags, A3 adds stair climbing, and A5 adds rain to the accounting.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's general thanks prompts A3's omitted effort; B4's stair-specific thanks prompts A5's weather addition.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 offer thanks but little independent need beyond feeding A another item to count.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds rain but introduces 'minutes' without an established meeting or record.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's shopping bags and A3's six flights twice make the work concrete.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's clipped tally works, but A5's meeting language adds an unsupported comic frame.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 78\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you call that a quick shop, I carried twelve bags up six flights.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I know. Sit down; I'll put everything away.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Thank you. The frozen peas came up separately. That was a second trip.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Then you sit down twice. I'll make tea.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you tell everyone why I'm getting two rests? Otherwise it looks like one long sit.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A seeks explicit acknowledgment of the effort and inconvenience contributed to a shared practical task.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking comfort or help after exertion is adjacent, but the card asks for recognition of the contribution itself.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 itemizes stair climbing; revised A5 asks B to explain the work behind the offered rests rather than merely provide relief.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a makes a helpful housemate's care become a request for public recognition; alternative b corrects a fence recipient's minimizing appraisal.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised in the same shopping setting, giving B helpful agency. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 counts the second trip; A5 requests acknowledgment), logic 5 (B2's rest prompts additional accounting; B4's two rests prompt an explanation), relationship 4 (B unpacks and offers tea), heightening 4 (private care becomes recognition to others), specificity 5 (peas, bags and six flights), brevityWit 4 (one long sit follows B4 exactly). Total 92; five spoken turns, 74 words, gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B4 is knowingly playful; actors should retain B's practical kindness so the exchange does not become two competing jokes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D33-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"e22b35bbd6a103e7ce4731cf755e97ef07e22cf46eee7347cb651045d39ee886\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 itemizes materials, errands and injury; A5 asks for the donated Saturday to be acknowledged explicitly.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's 'only three panels' prompts A3's expanded tally; B4's generic appreciation prompts A5's named acknowledgment.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 minimizes the repair, then B4 concedes appreciation, changing A's request from quantity to precision.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 makes successful appreciation insufficient until it includes the specific lost day established in A1.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's Saturday fence repair and A3's eighteen screws, two shops and blister are concrete and playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Saturday by name' compresses the demand for credit into a short, causally earned request.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I spent my Saturday fixing your fence.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's only three panels.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Three panels, eighteen screws, two shops and one blister.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll recommend you to next door. They've got six panels.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tell them three took my whole Saturday before you make me sound available for Sunday.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes the beneficiary acknowledge the full practical and temporal cost of A's fence repair.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Avoiding another repair is adjacent, but A's immediate demand is that B accurately describe the work already contributed.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 itemizes the completed labor; A5 asks B to include its full duration in B4's proposed recommendation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a turns a housemate's care into public acknowledgment; alternative b challenges praise that undervalues the labor and threatens to recruit more of it.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised B4 and A5 within the fence setting because generic thanks previously produced only a wording correction. Separate internal coach-1.0 reread: fidelity 5 (A3 inventories work; A5 requires its duration acknowledged), logic 5 (B2's minimization causes A3's tally; B4's referral causes A5's qualification), relationship 4 (B offers a recommendation while assuming availability), heightening 4 (A5 makes accurate acknowledgment matter to another day's demands), specificity 4 (A1's Saturday and B4's six panels), brevityWit 4 (A5's Sunday follows the referral). Total 90; five spoken ABABA turns, 53 words, all hard gates pass. Original firstPass preserved.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 also protects future free time; the request to tell the neighbors how long the completed repair took must remain the active recognition tactic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D34-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"026f29bf19c361f110e7b45d6fa02f0f6bb764dad054d6ffc494dca0f224337c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands a choice between dinner and a train, but A5 stops pressing an ordinary obligation and addresses the train figuratively.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2's quick eating meets A3's chicken timetable, though A1 says it is already burning; B4's choice yields only A5's tag.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 tries to preserve both plans and B4 chooses dinner, giving B a credible stake in the decision.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Tell the train' adds a joke after B4 resolves the choice rather than a playable consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies five minutes, but the relationship between saving dinner and reaching the train remains underexplained.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 personify chicken and train; the second personification does little practical work.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your parents' gravy needs stirring and you need a lift to the station. Which am I doing?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can't you leave dinner on a timer?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It won't stir the gravy. Do I finish their dinner or drive you?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Finish dinner. I'll book a taxi. Just carry my suitcase downstairs.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then choose again: suitcase downstairs now, or gravy without lumps for your parents?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A repeatedly makes B allocate A's immediate help between dinner duties and getting B to the station.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Complaining about being busy is adjacent, but A actively requires B to choose which ordinary obligation receives attention.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 rejects B2's timer because stirring still needs a person; A5 turns B4's suitcase request into another explicit allocation choice.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a lets a helpful taxi solution leave a smaller competing request for A's hands; alternative b renews collection pressure through the mother's incoming call.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the dinner/train candidate to remove the unestablished taxi-money dependency. Gravy needing continuous attention and suitcase carrying are the new illustrative details. Separate internal coach-1.0 reread: fidelity 5 (A1, A3 and A5 demand priorities), logic 5 (B2's timer prompts A3's stirring objection; B4's suitcase request supplies A5's exact conflict), relationship 4 (B arranges transport but still requests help), heightening 4 (A5 extends the priority demand into the remaining part of B4's solution), specificity 4 (A1's gravy and station; B4's downstairs luggage), brevityWit 4 (A5 makes the modest dinner consequence concrete). Total 90; five spoken ABABA turns, 71 words, all hard gates pass. Original firstPass preserved.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The gravy's urgency is A's insistence, and B could propose taking it off the heat; the scene leaves that ordinary negotiation open.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D34-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"668ca1531b9bcf79a250709447edd58eb91726039ba7b2688cff44debd6980d9\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 puts parcel collection beside collecting mother, and A3 presses limited capacity, though the urgency lacks concrete deadlines.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 insists both matter; A3 cites one car. B4 chooses parcel first, and A5 makes B own mother's demotion.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B wants both errands done while A controls the available car; B4's choice exposes a personal consequence.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds an insulting description of the choice but little new practical pressure after B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names the errands, but A3's lack of a trailer does not explain why sequential collection is impossible.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'second-class post' fits the parcel vocabulary but dominates the consequence with a prepared-sounding quip.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 73\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The parcel depot closes at six. Your mother's waiting outside the station. Which am I collecting?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The parcel's her birthday present.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then do you want her waiting for me or waiting for her present?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Get the parcel. I'll call her.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"She's calling me now. Shall I pull over to explain, or keep driving before the depot shuts?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes B choose which of two urgent collection duties receives the available driver and time.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Blaming someone for an unpopular choice is adjacent, but the active behavior must keep requesting a priority decision.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 converts B2's birthday explanation into a choice, and A5 makes answering mother's call compete with reaching the depot.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b ties both obligations to the same mother and asks B to own the time tradeoff; alternative a lets a helpful taxi plan generate a new coordination choice.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the collection setting, adding closing time, birthday context and an incoming call. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1, A3 and A5 require choices), logic 5 (B2 binds the errands; B4's promise to call meets mother's call to A), relationship 4 (B undertakes communication), heightening 4 (A5 makes explanation consume collection time), specificity 5 (six o'clock depot and station), brevityWit 4 (A3's two kinds of waiting). Total 92; five spoken turns, 73 words, gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The incoming call is conveniently timed, and the urgency works best if both understand the depot is nearly closing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D35-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0cddd2c843355ff38ced4a4466aeac87c248d47d58b91cc32562913f39f3d572\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 compares years of friendship with weeks of booking; A5 explicitly wants a commitment moved as proof of priority.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's long booking informs A3's longer relationship; B4's lunch-afterward solution makes A5 distinguish accommodation from rearrangement.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 values the appointment and B4 offers time together, so A must reveal the relational demand.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 exposes the stronger requirement after B4 solves the scheduling problem.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's haircut and lunch provide ordinary commitments that actors can understand immediately.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Useful comparison' and A5's 'not space around it' express A's sincere accounting of priority.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Move your haircut so we can have lunch.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've booked it for weeks.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We've been friends since school. Couldn't I have its place just once?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They charge twenty pounds if I change it today.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll pay. Put lunch in that exact slot, in pen. You've used pencil for me since school.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A seeks the displacement of B's established appointment as tangible proof that their friendship deserves priority.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simply securing lunch would permit any available time; A wants the appointment's protected place and permanence transferred to the friendship.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 asks for the haircut's place, and A5 offers to pay B4's change fee while requiring that exact slot in pen.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a incurs a financial cost to obtain a protected place in a friend's diary; alternative b accepts partial attendance but requires a sibling to give the relationship as the public reason.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the haircut scene so B4 supplies a concrete cost and A5 adopts a new bargaining tactic instead of explaining the original demand. The cancellation fee and friendship since school are new illustrative details. Separate internal coach-1.0 reread: fidelity 5 (A3 asks for displacement; A5 claims its exact slot), logic 5 (B2's established booking prompts A3's longer friendship; B4's fee causes A5's payment offer), relationship 4 (B protects an appointment and its cost), heightening 4 (A5 spends money and requests permanent diary status), specificity 4 (B4's twenty pounds and A5's pen), brevityWit 4 (A5's pencil history embodies the grievance). Total 90; five spoken ABABA turns, 62 words, all hard gates pass. Original firstPass preserved.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's pen-and-pencil distinction is polished, and the implied history of tentative plans arrives late; the payment offer supplies the concrete new tactic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D35-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"df984b69707cae0ad67de64588127c18debacd21acde8636f657f98b9296fb8a\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 asks B to skip quiz night; A3 compares being needed, but A5 leaves the relationship proof implicit.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's team need informs A3's competing need; B4's early departure informs A5's wish that the team notice.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 expresses loyalty to the team and B4 offers a compromise that A accepts.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Let them notice why' suggests a public consequence without specifying what B should make clear.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies quiz night but leaves the opening and A's relationship to B unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's competing claim on 'needing you' is economical, although A5's compression weakens clarity.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 75\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you leave quiz night for your sister's first exhibition opening?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm captain. They'll think I've abandoned them.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tell them your sister needs you. I'd like that to outrank geography.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll leave after round one and say I've got a headache.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Come after round one, but tell them it's for me. I want to rank above geography, not below a headache.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A asks B to rearrange a regular commitment and identify their relationship as the reason for doing so.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Wanting